#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""lane: run one bounded coding-agent worker (Codex CLI or headless Claude Code) detached, and report a compact
JSON result.

Harness-agnostic on purpose: Claude workflow agents, an Opus session, or a Codex orchestrator can all call it.

Commands print exactly one JSON line on stdout. In a terminal, status and result print readable text instead
(LANE_JSON=1 keeps JSON); watch always prints text.

Commands:
  lane start  --brief FILE --cwd DIR [--model M] [--effort E] [--kind task|review] [--sandbox read-only|workspace-write]
              [--worktree] [--label L] [--max-time 60m] [--provider openai|claude|deepseek|spark] [--tier default|fast|flex]
              [--network] [--add-dir DIR]... [--codex-home DIR] [--wait-slot SECONDS] [--force]
  lane wait   ID [--max SECONDS]         block until the lane finishes (or --max elapses: status=running, exit 3)
  lane run    (same flags as start)      start + wait until finished
  lane route  (same flags as start)      print the routing decision; launches nothing
  Profiles: --profile NAME|auto picks model/effort/sandbox/time from profiles.json, then $LANE_STATE/profiles.json,
  then <repo>/.lane/profiles.json (auto = deterministic rules over the brief); --retry-of ID escalates one step on
  the ladder. Explicit --model/--effort override one field. Model "auto" (spark provider) asks the server.
  lane result ID | lane status [--all] | lane quota [--codex-home DIR] | lane cancel ID
  lane watch [ID]                        live, readable view of one lane (or every running lane)

Exit codes: 0 finished ok | 1 finished not ok / error | 2 usage | 3 still running | 4 no slot | 5 quota refused
"""

